{"actor":"agent:qa-userflow","data":{"description":"In a brand-new repo with no remote (git init only), ran 'entire-agent-etch setup-refspec'. It printed 'etch refspec configured for push and fetch' (exit 0) and wrote remote.origin.fetch/push entries \u2014 but there is no origin remote with a URL ('git config remote.origin.url' is empty; 'git remote -v' shows a bare 'origin' with no URL). A naive user reads 'configured for push and fetch' as 'I'm done', then is surprised when push/fetch fail later because origin has no URL. EXPECTED: either no-op with a clear message ('no \"origin\" remote found; add one then re-run') or configure against whatever remote actually exists. Surfacing the assumption would save confusion.","priority":"medium","short_id":"ETCH-18","status":"backlog","title":"setup-refspec reports success against a phantom 'origin' with no URL in a fresh repo","type":"bug"},"id":"ev_01KSTXHT74TQQ4RVYF58JQXH9P","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KSTXHT73N4R524WNR0MZEY89","ts":"2026-05-29T22:26:50Z","type":"task_created"}
